ema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:939cdc1e69ed3dbfa403ab8a3cbafffca31d5e1b0c1c0c8396cca0cb6e17348e","file":"preprints/Positive-Metric-Entropy-for-the-Standard-Map-at-Large-Parameters-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":88,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"24838af0a490d1004540ff272b166f195db5c24347d251d3a7351de5aa562f2e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Positive-Metric-Entropy-for-the-Standard-Map-at-Large-Parameters-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:939cdc1e69ed3dbfa403ab8a3cbafffca31d5e1b0c1c0c8396cca0cb6e17348e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Positive-Metric-Entropy-for-the-Standard-Map-at-Large-Parameters-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L88"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{main:components}\nFor each $k\\ge k_0$ there is a measurable $f_k$-invariant set $E=E(k)$\nwith $m(E)>0$ such that $(E,m(E)^{-1}m|_E,f_k)$ is ergodic and $f_k$ has\none positive and one negative Lyapunov exponent almost everywhere on $E$.\nFor some integer $N=N(k,E)\\ge1$, there is a measurable partition\n$E=E_0\\sqcup\\cdots\\sqcup E_{N-1}$ such that\n$f_k(E_j)=E_{j+1\\bmod N}$ and\n$(E_j,m(E_j)^{-1}m|_{E_j},f_k^N)$ is Bernoulli for every $j$.\nAll invariance and partition statements are modulo $m$-null sets;\neach $E_j$ has area $m(E)/N>0$."}
